  "title": "Sebi Proposes Raising ISIN Cap and Easing Debt Listing Norms Amid Cybersecurity and Environmental Concerns",
  "summary": "Sebi has proposed raising the annual ISIN limit for private debt securities from 14 to 17 to ease funding constraints and reduce refinancing risks, while also addressing cybersecurity and environmental fraud. The proposed changes aim to streamline the process and reduce the impact of past debt issues.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Sebi has proposed raising the annual ISIN limit for private debt securities from 14 to 17 to ease funding constraints and reduce refinancing risks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sebi has also proposed to scrap mandatory listing of past debt issues to streamline the process.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A data breach at Framework Platforms and a fraud case against former Southern Water employees have emerged, highlighting concerns about cybersecurity and environmental accountability.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
